# Tersoff potential for monolayer GaS
# Parameter source: Y. Karaaslan, "Empirical interatomic potential development and
# classical molecular dynamics simulation of monolayer group-III monochalcogenides:
# insights into thermal transport properties", J. Phys. D: Appl. Phys. 58 (2025) 015306.
# One-body (n, beta): Table 1. Two-body (A, B, lambda1, lambda2): Table 2.
# Three-body (lambda3, c, d, h): Table 3. Cutoffs (R, D): Table S1 of the SI.
#
# Usage (units metal):
#   pair_style tersoff
#   pair_coeff * * GaS.tersoff Ga S
#
# Mapping notes (validated against the paper's relaxed EIAP geometry, SI Table S6:
# this file reproduces a0 = 3.835 A, d_Ga-Ga = 2.237 A, d_Ga-S = 2.409 A,
# h = 4.136 A exactly):
# - m = 3, gamma = 1: zeta term = fC(rik) * g(theta) * exp[lambda3^3 (rij - rik)^3],
#   identical to Eq. (S4)-(S6) of the paper.
# - n and beta are one-body parameters and follow the FIRST (center) element:
#   n(Ga) = 1.2088, beta(Ga) = 16.0491e-6; n(S) = 1.4114, beta(S) = 28.8467e-6.
# - A, B, lambda1, lambda2 of the Ga-S pair are used for both Ga-S and S-Ga rows.
# - The three-body (angular) parameters are keyed to the ordered (center atom i,
#   third atom k) pair, following GULP's pair-wise "boattractive" convention used
#   to fit the potential. Therefore the Ga-S-S set applies to entries Ga-S-S AND
#   Ga-Ga-S (i = Ga, k = S), and the S-Ga-Ga set applies to S-Ga-Ga AND S-S-Ga
#   (i = S, k = Ga). Triplet entries whose (i, k) pair is Ga-Ga or S-S carry no
#   fitted angular term and are switched off with gamma = 0 (placeholder c = 0,
#   d = 1 to avoid division by zero; they contribute nothing).
# - S-S pairs do not occur within the cutoff in this structure and were not
#   parameterized; the S-S two-body entry is disabled with A = B = 0.
# - R and D in each row gate the i-k distance of the zeta sum (and, in rows with
#   e2 = e3, the i-j pair cutoff). Ga-Ga: 3.00/0.15 A; Ga-S: 3.00/0.15 A.
#
# e1 e2 e3  m  gamma  lambda3      c            d        costheta0(h)  n       beta         lambda2  B          R     D     lambda1  A

